{
  "meta": {
    "version": 3,
    "updatedBy": "copilot",
    "note": "Windows Fluent UI for OpenClaw — ported from the v1 raw-CSS components.jsonc to v3 Auto Layout. WinUI-derived pixel padding is snapped to the nearest 4px spacing token; per-component notes record the source values and any approximation. Chat components track the native chat refresh in docs/CHAT_VISUAL_DESIGN.md and Themes/ChatResources.xaml (#1459): message and code surfaces use the `bubble` (12px) radius, the composer uses the `composer` (20px) radius, and chat binds the chat-local ChatResources brushes. Workspace-shell components (AgentIdentityBadge, ConnectionStatusFlyout, NotificationFlyout, WorkspaceShell) mirror the native Home and Sessions workspace shipped in #1541: WorkspaceWindow.xaml (Mica shell, left NavigationView, Owner footer), Controls/AgentIdentityBadge.xaml, Controls/GatewayStatusContent.xaml, and Controls/NotificationFlyoutContent.xaml are the source of truth; token bindings follow their ThemeResource keys."
  },
  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Button",
      "note": "Basic control. Primary action — one per view, where the eye should land. Previewed as `variant:primary`, the WinUI AccentButtonStyle: `accent` fill (AccentFillColorDefaultBrush) with `accentInk` text (TextOnAccentFillColorPrimaryBrush), `sm` radius (ControlCornerRadius). Hover = AccentFillColorSecondary (token `accentSubtle`); pressed = AccentFillColorTertiary (no exact token, previewed with `accentSubtle`, documented here); disabled = AccentFillColorDisabled with TextOnAccentFillColorDisabled (previewed as `control`/`muted`). The `variant:standard` Button swaps to the default ButtonStyle: `control` fill (ControlFillColorDefault), `controlLine` border (ControlStrokeColorDefault), `ink` text; hover ControlFillColorSecondary, pressed ControlFillColorTertiary, disabled ControlFillColorDisabled. Subtle/icon buttons are the separate SubtleButton block. Padding mirrors WinUI ButtonPadding (11,5,11,6), snapped to spacing tokens 3 (12≈11) and 1 (4≈5/6). In-app MinWidth 100px keeps short labels (OK / Connect) from cramping and gives side-by-side buttons a consistent footprint; that minimum has no spacing-token equivalent, so it stays a port note and the preview hugs its label.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Save changes",
        "variant": "primary"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "class": "ds-btn ds-btn-{variant}",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "padding": {
            "x": "3",
            "y": "1"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "accentInk",
          "background": "accent",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "pressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "control" }
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "TextBox",
      "note": "Basic control. Reusable default WinUI single-line TextBox, matching the stock control used by DirectUrlBox in Pages/ConnectionPage.xaml. Body text is 14px, the preview is 32px high with sm (4px) corners, and TextControlThemePadding is preserved exactly as 10,5,6,6 through named spacing tokens. Normal uses control/ink, pointer-over uses controlHover, and disabled uses controlDisabled/disabledText. The input has no separate native Pressed visual state: pressed previews retain pointer-over fill, while actual focus draws the 2px accent underline through control.focus. The browser uses controlLine as a flat approximation of TextControlElevationBorderBrush; native focused fill and the clear-button template remain owned by WinUI. Port as Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls.TextBox without replacing its template.",
      "props": {
        "accessibleName": "Text",
        "placeholder": "Enter text"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "textbox-input",
        "el": "input",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "text",
          "aria-label": "{accessibleName}",
          "placeholder": "{placeholder}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "padding": {
            "left": "textControlLeft",
            "top": "textControlTop",
            "right": "textControlEnd",
            "bottom": "textControlEnd"
          },
          "width": "fill",
          "height": 32
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "ink",
          "background": "control",
          "borderColor": "controlLine",
          "borderWidth": 1,
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "underline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "controlHover" },
          "pressed": { "background": "controlHover" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "controlHover" },
          "disabled": { "color": "disabledText", "background": "controlDisabled" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Field",
      "note": "Basic composition. A visible label above the shared TextBox control, separated by token 2 (8px), equivalent to a stock WinUI TextBox with Header and PlaceholderText. The Gateway address example passes its label as the TextBox accessible name and its placeholder through props. All input geometry and interaction states belong to TextBox, so this field and its instances stay aligned with the default control.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Gateway address",
        "placeholder": "127.0.0.1:18789"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "field-root",
        "el": "label",
        "class": "ds-field",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "vertical",
          "gap": "2",
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "field-label",
            "el": "span",
            "class": "ds-field-label",
            "appearance": {
              "fontFamily": "body",
              "textStyle": "body",
              "color": "ink"
            },
            "children": [
              "{label}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "field-input",
            "component": "TextBox",
            "props": {
              "accessibleName": "{label}",
              "placeholder": "{placeholder}"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Card",
      "note": "Content card. Flat by default: a 1px hairline border, not a drop shadow. Padding mirrors the WinUI Gallery card (16,12) as tokens 4 (16) and 3 (12) exactly, with the `md` radius and a `line`-colored border supplied by the ds-card class. The title binds `subtitle` (SubtitleTextBlockStyle, 20/28 SemiBold) and the description binds `body` (BodyTextBlockStyle, 14/20 Regular). Open report composes the shared HyperlinkButton, including its body typography and hover, pressed, disabled, and focus states. The card itself is static; only its action is interactive. Never nest a card inside a card.",
      "props": {
        "title": "Windows node",
        "body": "Paired · 6 capabilities exposed over MCP."
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "card-root",
        "el": "article",
        "class": "ds-card",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "vertical",
          "gap": "2",
          "padding": {
            "x": "4",
            "y": "3"
          },
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "card-title",
            "el": "h3",
            "class": "ds-card-title",
            "appearance": {
              "fontFamily": "display",
              "textStyle": "subtitle",
              "color": "ink"
            },
            "children": [
              "{title}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "card-body",
            "el": "p",
            "class": "ds-card-body",
            "appearance": {
              "fontFamily": "body",
              "textStyle": "body",
              "color": "muted"
            },
            "children": [
              "{body}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "card-link",
            "component": "HyperlinkButton",
            "props": {
              "children": "Open report"
            },
            "margin": {
              "top": "1"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Badge",
      "note": "Basic control. Status pill — a read-only, non-interactive label, so it carries no hover/pressed states. Uses semantic color tokens, never a raw hex: `positive` (SystemFillColorSuccess), `warning` (SystemFillColorCaution), `critical` (SystemFillColorCritical), or `muted` for neutral. Padding tokens 3/1 give the pill a compact footprint; the `pill` radius and tone color come from the ds-badge class. Two production relatives: the WorkspaceShell count badge is a Fluent InfoBadge (default pill geometry, framework fill), and the notification recurrence badge is a 10px-radius `warning` subtle-background chip with 7,1 padding — both non-interactive, documented on their host components.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Connected",
        "tone": "positive"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "badge-root",
        "el": "span",
        "class": "ds-badge ds-badge-{tone}",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "padding": {
            "x": "3",
            "y": "1"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SubtleButton",
      "note": "Basic control. Default WinUI SubtleButtonStyle, not the workspace's fixed-size icon variant. Uses native ButtonPadding 11,5,11,6 (left, top, right, bottom), a retained 1px ButtonBorderThemeThickness, sm (4px) ControlCornerRadius, and normal-weight 14px text. Width and height follow content; the style itself sets no 40x40 dimensions. Background, border, and foreground bind SubtleButton-specific normal, pointer-over, pressed, and disabled resources, including high-contrast overrides. Preview hover/pressed border tokens are transparent in light/dark: CSS paints the fill under the border, so adding the translucent native border again would produce an incorrect dark rim. High-contrast borders and keyboard focus remain visible. Disabled fill and border resolve to the same values as rest; disabled text uses TextFillColorDisabledBrush, not muted. Port with Style={StaticResource SubtleButtonStyle}, leaving the native template intact rather than copying the browser border compensation. Browser limitations: body uses a 20px line box; native system focus (FocusVisualMargin=-3) and the 83ms background transition are not reproduced by Colophon's shared renderer. Workspace icon sizing and padding overrides belong to usage variants.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Subtle button"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "subtle-button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "padding": {
            "left": "buttonHorizontal",
            "top": "buttonTop",
            "right": "buttonHorizontal",
            "bottom": "buttonBottom"
          },
          "width": "hug",
          "height": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "subtleButtonText",
          "background": "subtleButtonFill",
          "borderColor": "subtleButtonBorder",
          "borderWidth": 1,
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "color": "subtleButtonHoverText", "background": "subtleButtonHoverFill", "borderColor": "subtleButtonHoverBorder" },
          "pressed": { "color": "subtleButtonPressedText", "background": "subtleButtonPressedFill", "borderColor": "subtleButtonPressedBorder" },
          "hoverPressed": { "color": "subtleButtonPressedText", "background": "subtleButtonPressedFill", "borderColor": "subtleButtonPressedBorder" },
          "disabled": { "color": "subtleButtonDisabledText", "background": "subtleButtonFill", "borderColor": "subtleButtonBorder" }
        },
        "children": [
          "{label}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "HyperlinkButton",
      "note": "Basic control. WinUI HyperlinkButton used for inline navigation and quiet actions (Reconnect, Approve, Open Connection, Clear all, Open notifications). Accent link text (system accent hyperlink brush, token `accent`) with no border or fill at rest; hover shows the subtle wash (SubtleFillColorSecondary, `subtleHover`) and pressed deepens to SubtleFillColorTertiary (`subtlePressed`); disabled drops to `muted`. Horizontal padding mirrors the production `Padding=4,0` (token `1` left/right, no vertical pad); `sm` radius. Text uses the `body` scale. `control.chrome:none` strips the web button chrome; `control.focus` supplies the accent focus rectangle.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Open Connection"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "hyperlink-button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "padding": {
            "left": "1",
            "right": "1"
          },
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "accent",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "subtleHover" },
          "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "$none" }
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ToggleSwitch",
      "note": "Basic control. Static WinUI ToggleSwitch track reference, shown On for the existing settings composition pending interactive renderer support. Native geometry is 40x20 with a 12x12 resting knob, 14x14 pointer-over knob, and 17x14 pressed knob. Props describe a frozen snapshot, not live state. Colophon cannot persist checked state or animate geometry, so this is an image rather than a misleading non-working switch button. Native On/Off uses RepositionThemeAnimation with 20px travel; resizing uses 83ms and spline 0,0,0,1, except Disabled at 250ms. Full header/content layout, dragging, focus, keyboard switching, and CircleElevationBorderBrush remain native behavior. See DESIGN.md for bindings and limitations.",
      "props": {
        "label": "On, normal. Static ToggleSwitch reference.",
        "trackFill": "accent",
        "trackStroke": "toggleOnStroke",
        "knobFill": "accentInk",
        "knobX": 23.5,
        "knobY": 4,
        "knobWidth": 12,
        "knobHeight": 12
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "toggle-switch-root",
        "el": "svg",
        "attrs": {
          "viewBox": "0 0 40 20",
          "width": 40,
          "height": 20,
          "role": "img",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": { "width": 40, "height": 20 },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "toggle-switch-track",
            "el": "rect",
            "attrs": { "width": 40, "height": 20, "rx": 10, "fill": "var(--color-{trackFill})" }
          },
          {
            "id": "toggle-switch-stroke",
            "el": "rect",
            "attrs": { "x": 0.5, "y": 0.5, "width": 39, "height": 19, "rx": 9.5, "fill": "none", "stroke": "var(--color-{trackStroke})", "stroke-width": 1 }
          },
          {
            "id": "toggle-switch-thumb",
            "el": "rect",
            "attrs": { "x": "{knobX}", "y": "{knobY}", "width": "{knobWidth}", "height": "{knobHeight}", "rx": 7, "fill": "var(--color-{knobFill})" }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "StatusDot",
      "note": "Basic control. The 10x10 connection/status indicator reused in the gateway flyout (Ellipse), the workspace Owner footer (10px FontIcon), and the identity badges. Non-interactive, so no hover/pressed states. Fill is a semantic token; previewed `positive` (SystemFillColorSuccess) for connected, and the variants are `warning` (SystemFillColorCaution) attention, `critical` (SystemFillColorCritical) error, and `muted`/neutral unknown. 10px sits between spacing tokens (nearest `2`=8); previewed at a literal 10x10 with a `pill` radius.",
      "props": {
        "tone": "positive"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "status-dot-root",
        "el": "span",
        "attrs": {
          "role": "img",
          "aria-label": "Connected"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "width": 10,
          "height": 10
        },
        "appearance": {
          "background": "positive",
          "radius": "pill"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Avatar",
      "note": "Basic control. Default WinUI PersonPicture initials reference: 96x96, a 1px ellipse stroke, PersonPictureEllipseFillThemeBrush, primary foreground, and SemiBold initials at diameter * 0.42 = 40.32px. ContentControlThemeFontFamily, not the Caption style. No hover or pressed states: PersonPicture is not interactive. AvatarStates shows Contact and People glyph fallbacks. Photo clipping, automatic initials, badges, and native TextLineBounds=Tight remain native behavior. Existing 32px agent and 24px owner avatars are usage overrides, not this control's defaults.",
      "props": {
        "initials": "AU",
        "name": "Example user"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "avatar-root",
        "el": "span",
        "attrs": {
          "role": "img",
          "aria-label": "{name}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "width": 96,
          "height": 96
        },
        "appearance": {
          "textStyle": "personInitials",
          "color": "nativeText",
          "background": "personPictureFill",
          "borderColor": "personPictureStroke",
          "borderWidth": 1,
          "radius": "pill"
        },
        "children": [
          "{initials}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "AvatarStates",
      "note": "PersonPicture's native initials, NoPhotoOrInitials (Contact U+E77B), and Group (People U+E716) presentations. All are static and non-focusable. Photo and badge states require native image/initials handling and are not claimed by these references.",
      "root": {
        "id": "avatar-states-root",
        "el": "div",
        "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "6", "wrap": true },
        "children": [
          { "id": "avatar-initials", "component": "Avatar" },
          { "id": "avatar-contact", "component": "Avatar", "props": { "initials": "\uE77B", "name": "Person without photo or initials" }, "appearance": { "textStyle": "personSymbol" } },
          { "id": "avatar-group", "component": "Avatar", "props": { "initials": "\uE716", "name": "Group" }, "appearance": { "textStyle": "personSymbol" } }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "InfoBar",
      "note": "Basic control. Native InfoBar horizontal reference, shown Error. Severity changes BOTH background and layered 16px icon; InfoBarStates shows all four. Native title is 14px SemiBold and message 14px Normal, both primary foreground. ControlCornerRadius=4; content-grid minimum height=48 plus outer border; leading padding=16, icon gap=14, text top=14, title/message gap=12, panel end margin=16. Close uses InfoBarCloseButtonStyle (DefaultButtonStyle with AppBarButton resources), 38x38 plus margin 5, with a 16px Cancel glyph. Hover/press/disabled/focus visuals work, but close does NOT dismiss: the renderer has no dismiss action. Native responsive InfoBarPanel, conditional content and high-contrast 2px border are unsupported; browser wrapping and the 1px preview border are not 1:1 native proof.",
      "props": {
        "title": "Couldn't reach the gateway",
        "message": "Check that the gateway is running, then retry.",
        "iconTone": "infoErrorIcon",
        "iconGlyph": "\uF13D"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "info-bar-root",
        "el": "div",
        "attrs": { "role": "status" },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "padding": { "left": "4" },
          "align": "start",
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "background": "infoErrorFill",
          "borderColor": "infoBorder",
          "borderWidth": 1,
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "info-bar-icon",
            "el": "svg",
            "attrs": {
              "aria-hidden": "true",
              "viewBox": "0 0 16 16",
              "width": 16,
              "height": 16
            },
            "layout": { "width": 16, "height": 16 },
            "margin": { "top": "4", "right": "infoIconGap", "bottom": "4" },
            "appearance": { "textStyle": "infoSymbol" },
            "children": [
              { "id": "info-bar-icon-background", "el": "text", "attrs": { "x": 8, "y": 8, "text-anchor": "middle", "dominant-baseline": "central", "fill": "var(--color-{iconTone})" }, "children": [ "\uF136" ] },
              { "id": "info-bar-icon-foreground", "el": "text", "attrs": { "x": 8, "y": 8, "text-anchor": "middle", "dominant-baseline": "central", "fill": "var(--color-infoIconForeground)" }, "children": [ "{iconGlyph}" ] }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "info-bar-text",
            "el": "div",
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "3", "wrap": true, "grow": true },
            "margin": { "top": "infoTextTop", "right": "4" },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "info-bar-title",
                "el": "span",
                "appearance": { "fontFamily": "body", "textStyle": "bodyStrong", "color": "nativeText" },
                "children": [ "{title}" ]
              },
              {
                "id": "info-bar-message",
                "el": "span",
                "appearance": { "fontFamily": "body", "textStyle": "body", "color": "nativeText" },
                "children": [ "{message}" ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "info-bar-close",
            "el": "button",
            "attrs": { "type": "button", "aria-label": "Close (visual reference only)", "title": "Visual states only. Dismissal is not supported by this renderer." },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "align": "center", "justify": "center", "width": 38, "height": 38 },
            "margin": "buttonTop",
            "appearance": { "color": "nativeText", "background": "$none", "borderColor": "$none", "borderWidth": 1, "radius": "sm" },
            "control": {
              "chrome": "none",
              "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
            },
            "states": {
              "hover": { "background": "infoCloseHoverFill", "color": "infoCloseHoverText" },
              "pressed": { "background": "infoClosePressedFill", "color": "infoClosePressedText" },
              "hoverPressed": { "background": "infoClosePressedFill", "color": "infoClosePressedText" },
              "disabled": { "background": "$none", "color": "subtleButtonDisabledText" }
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "info-bar-close-glyph",
                "el": "span",
                "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" },
                "appearance": { "textStyle": "infoSymbol" },
                "children": [ "\uE711" ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "InfoBarStates",
      "note": "Native severity references. Each reuses InfoBar's geometry, typography, layered glyph, and close-control states. The body remains static; severity is not a hover state. No close/dismiss behavior is implemented by Colophon.",
      "root": {
        "id": "info-bar-states-root",
        "el": "div",
        "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "3", "width": "fill" },
        "children": [
          { "id": "info-bar-informational", "component": "InfoBar", "props": { "title": "Informational", "message": "Gateway settings are ready to review.", "iconTone": "infoAttentionIcon", "iconGlyph": "\uF13F" }, "appearance": { "background": "infoAttentionFill" } },
          { "id": "info-bar-success", "component": "InfoBar", "props": { "title": "Success", "message": "The gateway is connected.", "iconTone": "infoSuccessIcon", "iconGlyph": "\uF13E" }, "appearance": { "background": "infoSuccessFill" } },
          { "id": "info-bar-warning", "component": "InfoBar", "props": { "title": "Warning", "message": "Pairing approval is required.", "iconTone": "infoWarningIcon", "iconGlyph": "\uF13C" }, "appearance": { "background": "infoWarningFill" } },
          { "id": "info-bar-error", "component": "InfoBar", "props": { "title": "Error", "message": "The gateway could not be reached." } }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPicker",
      "note": "ReactorChatComposer.PickerButton at production 9e4999c6: a native Button with toolbar resource overrides, not a ComboBox. Native label 13px, ChevronDown U+E70D at 12px, 4px label-to-chevron gap, 8px horizontal and 4px vertical padding, 32px minimum height, 4px corners and no border. ChatSecondaryTextBrush supplies rest text. Model and effort are right-aligned in Workspace; only standalone ChatWindow includes a session trigger. The browser opens a representative option list, not the production searchable model flyout or effort slider. Native label trimming, 44px compact targets and the narrow effort gauge remain port requirements.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Model"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button",
          "aria-haspopup": "listbox",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "gap": "1",
          "padding": {
            "left": "2",
            "right": "2",
            "top": "1",
            "bottom": "1"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "height": 32,
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "textStyle": "chatPicker",
          "color": "chatSecondary",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "subtleHover", "color": "subtleButtonHoverText" },
          "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed", "color": "subtleButtonPressedText" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed", "color": "subtleButtonPressedText" },
          "disabled": { "color": "disabledText", "background": "$none" }
        },
        "on": { "click": { "open": "ComposerPickerOptions" } },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-label",
            "el": "span",
            "children": [
              "{label}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-chevron",
            "el": "span",
            "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" },
            "appearance": { "textStyle": "chatChevron" },
            "children": [ "\uE70D" ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPickerOptions",
      "note": "Representative single-select flyout for the subtle composer pickers (model, session, reasoning-effort). Ships as a WinUI Flyout of RadioMenuItem rows on a `surface` (CardBackgroundFillColorDefault) sheet with 12px (`lg`) overlay corners (ChatPickerFlyoutStyle, #1459) and `md` shadow. Each row reserves a leading glyph column; the selected row shows an `accent` Segoe Fluent Icons CheckMark (glyph U+E73E, WinUI SymbolThemeFontFamily selection glyph, not a radio dot) while unselected rows keep the column empty so labels stay aligned. The check glyph carries a font-family-only raw style because the icon font is outside the display/body/mono token set (documented as the `icon` typography family in design.json); color stays token-bound to `accent`. Selecting a row closes the flyout; reopening restores defaults. Because `on.click.open` targets take no props, this shows a representative model list; the real model picker (AutoSuggestBox over a grouped ListView) and the effort slider/gauge are supplied by the app and are a Reactor port note.",
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-options",
        "el": "div",
        "attrs": { "role": "menu", "aria-label": "Model" },
        "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "1", "padding": "1", "width": "hug" },
        "appearance": { "background": "surface", "color": "ink", "textStyle": "small", "radius": "lg", "shadow": "md" },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "composer-option-sonnet",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "true" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
              { "id": "composer-option-sonnet-check", "el": "span", "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true", "style": "font-family:'Segoe Fluent Icons','Segoe MDL2 Assets',sans-serif" }, "layout": { "width": 16 }, "appearance": { "color": "accent", "textAlign": "center" }, "children": ["\uE73E"] },
              "Claude Sonnet 5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-option-opus",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "false" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
              { "id": "composer-option-opus-check", "el": "span", "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" }, "layout": { "width": 16 } },
              "Claude Opus 4.8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-option-gpt",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "false" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
              { "id": "composer-option-gpt-check", "el": "span", "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" }, "layout": { "width": 16 } },
              "GPT-5.6"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ChatBubble",
      "note": "Bubbleless assistant turn from ReactorChatTimeline and ChatMarkdownPresentation at production 9e4999c6. This reference shows the below-960px chat viewport variant without an avatar, at the 736px prose cap (768 minus two 16px insets). Native prose is 14/21, with 16px between blocks and 4px vertical content padding. The footer is sender, time, model and usage at 12/18, followed by 32x32 Copy and Read aloud controls with 14px Fluent glyphs. Copy is always visible. Read aloud previews the native 70% resting opacity through chatReadAloudText, returning to full alpha over the button; native row-level hover is not represented. Native avatars appear in a separate 44px gutter above the 960px breakpoint; do not replace the production logo with an invented sparkle. ChatTextBrush and ChatSecondaryTextBrush preserve alpha. The native source remains authoritative for Markdown, responsive layout, clipboard and speech behavior.",
      "props": {
        "sender": "Assistant",
        "time": "2:14 PM",
        "model": "browse",
        "usage": "12.5K/200K (6%)",
        "children": "FIXTURE MAIN: the lighthouse is green."
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "chat-bubble-root",
        "el": "div",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "gap": "2",
          "align": "start",
          "width": 736
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "chat-bubble-stack",
            "el": "div",
            "layout": {
              "mode": "vertical",
              "gap": "1",
              "align": "start",
              "grow": true
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "chat-bubble-message",
                "el": "div",
                "layout": {
                  "mode": "vertical",
                  "gap": "4",
                  "padding": { "y": "1" },
                  "width": "fill"
                },
                "appearance": {
                  "textStyle": "chatProse",
                  "color": "chatText"
                },
                "children": [
                  "{children}"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "chat-bubble-footer",
                "el": "div",
                "layout": {
                  "mode": "horizontal",
                  "gap": "1",
                  "align": "center"
                },
                "margin": { "top": "1" },
                "appearance": {
                  "textStyle": "chatFooter",
                  "color": "chatSecondary"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "chat-bubble-identity",
                    "el": "span",
                    "margin": { "right": "1" },
                    "children": [
                      "{sender} · {time} · {model} · {usage}"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "chat-bubble-copy",
                    "component": "ChatCopyButton"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "chat-bubble-readaloud",
                    "el": "button",
                    "attrs": {
                      "type": "button",
                      "title": "Read aloud",
                      "aria-label": "Read message aloud"
                    },
                    "layout": {
                      "mode": "horizontal",
                      "align": "center",
                      "justify": "center",
                      "width": 32,
                      "height": 32,
                      "padding": "0"
                    },
                    "appearance": {
                      "color": "chatReadAloudText",
                      "background": "$none",
                      "radius": "sm"
                    },
                    "control": { "chrome": "none", "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" } },
                    "states": {
                      "hover": { "background": "subtleHover", "color": "chatSecondary" },
                      "pressed": { "background": "chatReadAloudPressed", "color": "chatSecondary" },
                      "hoverPressed": { "background": "chatReadAloudPressed", "color": "chatSecondary" }
                    },
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "chat-bubble-readaloud-glyph",
                        "el": "span",
                        "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" },
                        "appearance": { "textStyle": "chatActionIcon" },
                        "children": [ "\uE767" ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ChatUserBubble",
      "note": "Sent user bubble from ReactorChatTimeline.BuildUser at production 9e4999c6. Native ChatUserBrush is the system accent at 8% in Light and 12% in Dark, not a solid blue card. Text uses ChatUserTextBrush (primary text; highlight text in HC), 14/21, with 16px horizontal and 12px vertical padding, no stroke and 12px corners. The native width is content-sized and capped at 720px. The shared 32px Copy action sits below with 8px of stack spacing plus the native 2px top and 4px trailing margin, preserving the measured 10px gap for a sent message. Hover-only native metadata and queued-message states are not reproduced by this sent-message reference.",
      "props": { "children": "Can we browse the synthetic Gateway?" },
      "root": {
        "id": "chat-user-root",
        "el": "div",
        "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "2", "align": "end", "width": "hug" },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "chat-user-surface",
            "el": "div",
            "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "2", "padding": { "x": "4", "y": "3" } },
            "appearance": { "textStyle": "chatProse", "background": "chatUser", "color": "chatUserText", "radius": "bubble" },
            "children": [ "{children}" ]
          },
          {
            "id": "chat-user-copy",
            "component": "ChatCopyButton",
            "margin": { "top": "half", "right": "1" }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ChatComposer",
      "note": "Workspace composer from ReactorChatComposer at production 9e4999c6, measured against the Release app and fixture Gateway. Reference width 768px, resting outer height 112px, 20px radius, 1px ChatStrokeBrush, native alpha-preserving ChatComposerBrush card fill. Inner padding is 16,12,16,8; input is at least 44px tall with 16px text and no padding, fill, border or accent underline, including focus. Stack gap 8px. Attach is the native paperclip U+E723, not Add. Workspace omits the session selector; model and effort align right before Voice and circular 32px Send. Toolbar glyphs are native 16px Segoe Fluent Icons. Preview contains a draft so Send is enabled; typing does not send, auto-grow, or update Send eligibility. Empty/disabled, Stop, narrow gauge, native flyouts and dynamic input behavior remain production responsibilities. At native widths <=560 effort uses a 44px gauge; the installed renderer cannot express that responsive switch. The reading cap, 40px/12px outer gutters and 12px vertical margin belong to the host, not this isolated writing-surface component.",
      "props": {
        "placeholder": "Message Assistant (Enter to send)",
        "draft": "Draft for visual comparison",
        "model": "Fixture Browse",
        "effort": "off"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "chat-composer-root",
        "el": "div",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "vertical",
          "gap": "2",
          "padding": { "left": "4", "top": "3", "right": "4", "bottom": "2" },
